add([1322,1323],'mean-seven-error','Six-child mean versus seven displayed rows','The next population is [C1′,C2,C3,C4,C5,C6]; unmutated C1 is only a comparison row. Their exact fitnesses are [1/12,1/12,1/24,1/34,1/45,1/34]. What is the population mean rounded to four decimals?',[
('0.0482.','Sum exactly the six actual members and divide by6.'),('0.0473.','This results from also counting unmutated C1 with fitness1/24 and dividing by7.'),('0.0428.','That is the original population mean, not the new one.'),('0.0833.','That is the best individual fitness rather than the mean.')], 'The source’s0.0473 matches an average over seven displayed rows including the replaced unmutated child. The six-member new population has mean0.0482298475.',typ='numerical',difficulty='medium',kind='table',steps=['Sum2/12+1/24+2/34+1/45.','Divide the sum by6 to obtain0.0482298475.','Round once at the end to0.0482.'],formulas=[FM],conflict='The comparison slide gives generation-one mean0.0473, consistent with counting the unmutated comparison row as a seventh member.',locator='Seven displayed evaluation rows versus six-child generation comparison.')
